{"title":"2017 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Not_Very_Fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Not Very Fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_the_RMM_Club\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by the RMM Club</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the figure below, choose point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> have equal perimeters. What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53eb67d35ecca7ac6f68e8dff60b0eb5f3e4a602.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]draw((0,0)--(4,0)--(0,3)--(0,0)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,0), SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (4,0), ESE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (0, 3), N); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (0, 1.5), W); label(&quot;$4$&quot;, (2, 0), S); label(&quot;$5$&quot;, (2, 1.5), NE);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"198\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c2a671715d10f7e5fc108be1af7c48411907176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{3}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{3}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }2\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{12}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"377\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that the perimeters of the two small triangles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c9baf49e329e4da7080a38964943e1968e7824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+CD+AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c66b39f52c2df8bba0e7f3c9765624b37f4b59d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+BD+AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />. Setting both equal and using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/7211af31ccf32bcb08df8e89df65a86ce9b129df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD+CD = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"115\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0ae22fbe6167df969d0b1f9a698029e6774c45a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 2$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/3/b53e0064e5c0075ceeb38a4e29b4fa1ed396dd85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 3$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />. Now, we simply have to find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d8856a7429d98abb14ef48fc8550c0375408cec7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BD}{CD} = \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adbd8883f0cd8632fcfbbf06047ae4d60076fef4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[ABD]}{[ACD]} = 2/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"111\" height=\"45\" />. Combining this with the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8610994146054d34d9933863709ec1574f11f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC] = [ABD] + [ACD] = \\frac{3\\cdot4}{2} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"299\" height=\"37\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5e715c3874487c0abd4ed1151a562b3058d244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABD] = \\frac{2}{5}[ABC] = \\frac{2}{5} \\cdot 6 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{12}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"299\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> to equate the perimeter. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0df2e23d9b77571d16702df49c13bcaef3ceadeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}+\\overline{BD}+1=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8988e53e2169771bcd65adfe974dc0f692c8d674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a260f433b5f08865db7182564b27c3f37bca39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2)(4)(\\sin B)}{2}=4(\\frac{3}{5})=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{12}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"261\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~megaboy6679\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Not_Very_Fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Not_Very_Fast)\">Solution 3 (Not Very Fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Not Very Fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Letting point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> we get point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86f58cb609fa753024f1173510c877971f8e4e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b8eb8e093d1d1c3834d880a7b448b3fa76eeab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> has a slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/dee6596f6d34c586070c53b458cf129f8c513e05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> and it has intercepts the y-axis at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b8eb8e093d1d1c3834d880a7b448b3fa76eeab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> so the equation for line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc4b96e4d30c60774375b12566a3454f69636111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{3}{4}x+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" />. Using the same methods from Solution 1 and Solution 2 you can find out that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The equation of a circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b8eb8e093d1d1c3834d880a7b448b3fa76eeab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b9ec1f7d3659ed138a19de8a5394347df4c640c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+(y-3)^2=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"21\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/3459c70675fe917e46fbe771d77377ed2c7a5b6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+(-\\frac{3}{4}x)^2=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"38\" />. Simplifying it you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a406167eb8ff9792c88a14c539fed7a4ba0eee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+\\frac{9}{16}x^2=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" />. Multiplying it my <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and adding you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54eec8a0c7b14b0bc83ddc418f67ed9122c03e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25x^2=144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" /> which becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/4/38449b446f06537d3af0e63c02462321b8d7e89c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=12/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> after solving for the positive answer. You can then plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/4/38449b446f06537d3af0e63c02462321b8d7e89c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=12/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> back into the slope intercept equation and you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d3f6b940dbbd3fe4531b5f8571f9ad79520ea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{3}{4}(\\frac{12}{5})+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" /> which becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/843d3be1a61569f04ea0c0f3531841205496e14e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=6/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />. Letting that be the height you can see that the base is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/4127e4ef187b25a0bf2385fbfb9964c9825c5a96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{6}{5})(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"65\" height=\"38\" />. Which becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2edfbd1849e04ee24bd1fd73857a060fa3c1b0f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{12}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"71\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>Note: This uses coordinate geometry which could be useful when you don't know how to solve a geometric problem\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_the_RMM_Club\">Video Solution by the RMM Club</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by the RMM Club\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/itz3JyoZQYg\">https://youtu.be/itz3JyoZQYg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/in